   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Was y were",
    "@en": "Was and were"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "El pasado de «to be» tiene dos formas. **Was** va con I, he, she, it: **I was at home** (estaba en casa). **Were** va con you, we, they: **They were at work**.",
     "@en": "The past of «to be» has two forms. **Was** goes with I, he, she, it: **I was at home** (I was at home). **Were** goes with you, we, they: **They were at work**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Negación: **wasn't** y **weren't**. Pregunta: **Were you at home?** — **Yes, I was** / **No, I wasn't**.",
     "@en": "Denial: **wasn't** and **weren't**. Question: **Were you at home?**-**Yes, I was** / **No, I wasn't**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para nacer se usa siempre el pasado: **I was born in Madrid** (nací en Madrid).",
     "@en": "The past is always used to be born: **I was born in Madrid** (born in Madrid)."
    }
   ]
  },
